contentText:
Justin Timberlake has countless hits on his résumé, 39 Billboard Hot 100 entries as a solo artist and 13 more as a part of *NSYNC.

JT sat down with Complex on Thursday (Nov. 5) to reminisce on his decorated catalog and rank the best songs of his career, and he ultimately went with &#8220;What Goes Around&#8230;/&#8230; Comes Around,&#8221; which topped the Billboard Hot 100 in March 2007 and landed on Timberlake&#8217;s FutureSex/LoveSounds album.

&#8220;I would put this at No. 1 or No. 2,&#8221; he said. &#8220;It&#8217;s the first song I wrote for FutureSex/LoveSounds . Maybe I should dispel a rumor at this point, which has gone around forever, which it&#8217;s not a personal story of mine; it&#8217;s actually a personal story from a friend.&#8221;

Timberlake continued: &#8220;He was going through it and telling me what had happened. I said, &#8216;Do you mind if I write about this?&#8217; And I quote, my friend said, &#8216;Yeah, torch that bi&#8212;. What goes around comes around.&#8217; I was like, &#8216;I have to go. Thank you, I have to go.'&#8221;

It has long been rumored that &#8220;What Goes Around&#8230;/&#8230;Comes Around&#8221; was inspired by his close friend Juan &#8220;Trace&#8221; Ayala&#8217;s fractured relationship with The Girl Next Door actress Elisha Cuthbert.

&#8220;I just went in and again, this song was written in damn near 20 minutes,&#8221; JT added. &#8220;It was just flowing. The interlude that goes with it and then you put the video with it,&#8221; he said, referencing the Scarlett Johansson-starring clip. &#8220;We shot a 10-minute video we shot for it. This just hit on all cylinders for me.&#8221;

Timberlake gave &#8220;What Goes Around&#8221; the nod over &#8220;Mirrors,&#8221; &#8220;My Love,&#8221; &#8220;SexyBack&#8221; and &#8220;Cry Me a River&#8221; to round out his personal top five.

Elsewhere in the interview, Timberlake opened up about how Ye told him that &#8220;SexyBack&#8221; inspired him to make &#8220;Stronger,&#8221; which saw West bring in Timbaland to get the drums correct on his Graduation smash.

&#8220;You could probably find it, Kanye came to one of the shows on the FutureSex/LoveShow Tour. I had him come up and we did &#8216;Stronger&#8217; together,&#8221; JT recalled. &#8220;He showed up and was suited up like I was. It was a moment. I remember talking a lot about that song.&#8221;

As for the future, Timberlake revealed that he worked on a few songs with Don Toliver after popping out at the &#8220;Can&#8217;t Say&#8221; rapper&#8217;s Miami tour stop in August. Toliver sampled JT&#8217;s &#8220;Rock Your Body&#8221; on his OCTANE standout &#8220;BODY.&#8221;

&#8220;I was like, &#8216;Don&#8217;t you have a studio on the road?&#8217; He was like, &#8216;Yeah.&#8217; I was like, &#8216;Cool, take a shower. Let&#8217;s work.&#8217; We stayed at the arena for a couple hours. We did a few ideas,&#8221; he teased.

